Protein name: Lysozyme
Organism: Bombyx mori
PDB ID: 1GD6
Experimental method (X-ray, Cryo-EM, NMR, etc.): X-ray diffraction
Resolution (if available): 2.50 Å
Biological significance: Lysozyme is an enzyme that damages bacterial cell walls by catalyzing the hydrolysis of bonds between sugars in peptidoglycan.
